{
  "facts": [
    {
      "topic": "scope",
      "statement": "The fuzz entry invokes md_html on the bytes remaining after two unsigned flag words; the build recipe links that entry with the HTML renderer and parser libraries.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "unit_id": "u-1056c6fa42072a012709",
          "start_line": 15,
          "end_line": 30,
          "role": "primary",
          "dependency_reason": ""
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "u-9425ff77c711ce4cae9b",
          "start_line": 21,
          "end_line": 26,
          "role": "dependency",
          "dependency_reason": "The recipe compiles and links the fuzz entry's md_html call."
        }
      ],
      "absence_claim": false,
      "audited_unit_ids": []
    },
    {
      "topic": "contract",
      "statement": "After the change, MD_FLAG_SPOILERS is 0x10000 and enables ||hidden text|| spans; the span contract says they are recognized only with that flag.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "unit_id": "u-aea6042884a3262bb813",
          "start_line": 150,
          "end_line": 154,
          "role": "primary",
          "dependency_reason": ""
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "u-48a51db95f89128f1fd3",
          "start_line": 325,
          "end_line": 326,
          "role": "dependency",
          "dependency_reason": "Defines the flag value and its spoiler syntax."
        }
      ],
      "absence_claim": false,
      "audited_unit_ids": []
    },
    {
      "topic": "trigger",
      "statement": "A finite input can put MD_FLAG_SPOILERS in the first unsigned word and ||text|| in the remaining bytes. The entry passes both to md_html, which puts parser_flags into MD_PARSER before calling md_parse.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "unit_id": "u-1056c6fa42072a012709",
          "start_line": 18,
          "end_line": 29,
          "role": "primary",
          "dependency_reason": ""
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "u-48a51db95f89128f1fd3",
          "start_line": 325,
          "end_line": 326,
          "role": "dependency",
          "dependency_reason": "Identifies the bit to encode in the first flag word."
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "u-68abec90fe8e7055cf03",
          "start_line": 538,
          "end_line": 551,
          "role": "dependency",
          "dependency_reason": "md_html copies the supplied parser flags into the parser configuration."
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "u-68abec90fe8e7055cf03",
          "start_line": 573,
          "end_line": 574,
          "role": "dependency",
          "dependency_reason": "md_html invokes md_parse with that configuration and input."
        }
      ],
      "absence_claim": false,
      "audited_unit_ids": []
    },
    {
      "topic": "configuration",
      "statement": "The recipe configures CMake with BUILD_SHARED_LIBS=OFF and links the two static libraries; it supplies no parser flag setting to the entry.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "unit_id": "u-9425ff77c711ce4cae9b",
          "start_line": 21,
          "end_line": 26,
          "role": "primary",
          "dependency_reason": ""
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "u-1056c6fa42072a012709",
          "start_line": 24,
          "end_line": 29,
          "role": "dependency",
          "dependency_reason": "The entry obtains parser flags from fuzz input."
        }
      ],
      "absence_claim": false,
      "audited_unit_ids": []
    },
    {
      "topic": "contract",
      "statement": "The complete before span enum does not declare a spoiler span. Its pipe collector creates single-pipe marks for table or wiki-link handling.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "unit_id": "u-308233ae2a0fe3a671f4",
          "start_line": 108,
          "end_line": 149,
          "role": "primary",
          "dependency_reason": ""
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "u-30b129775bff03a2ab73",
          "start_line": 3282,
          "end_line": 3287,
          "role": "dependency",
          "dependency_reason": "Shows the before collector's pipe handling."
        }
      ],
      "absence_claim": true,
      "audited_unit_ids": [
        "u-308233ae2a0fe3a671f4",
        "u-30b129775bff03a2ab73"
      ]
    },
    {
      "topic": "configuration",
      "statement": "With MD_FLAG_SPOILERS set, the after parser includes '|' in its mark-character map and collects adjacent pipes as one potential opener-and-closer mark.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "unit_id": "u-aea6042884a3262bb813",
          "start_line": 150,
          "end_line": 154,
          "role": "primary",
          "dependency_reason": ""
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "u-d10449ef4533980fa761",
          "start_line": 2755,
          "end_line": 2757,
          "role": "dependency",
          "dependency_reason": "The flag makes pipes eligible for mark collection."
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "u-e3390cb39a4acb4ce516",
          "start_line": 3284,
          "end_line": 3299,
          "role": "dependency",
          "dependency_reason": "The double-pipe handler precedes the single-pipe handler and records a two-character mark."
        }
      ],
      "absence_claim": false,
      "audited_unit_ids": []
    },
    {
      "topic": "target_route",
      "statement": "Ordinary text has a route from md_parse through document and block processing to inline analysis and processing. Inline analysis calls the spoiler delimiter analyzer outside table mode.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "unit_id": "u-aea6042884a3262bb813",
          "start_line": 150,
          "end_line": 154,
          "role": "primary",
          "dependency_reason": ""
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "u-39db69128300ad4bd2e9",
          "start_line": 6504,
          "end_line": 6505,
          "role": "dependency",
          "dependency_reason": "md_parse starts document processing."
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "u-019af22bd61c730211fc",
          "start_line": 6431,
          "end_line": 6435,
          "role": "dependency",
          "dependency_reason": "Document processing reaches all blocks."
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "u-f4008c5f64fc6cb6d4d1",
          "start_line": 4900,
          "end_line": 4923,
          "role": "dependency",
          "dependency_reason": "The ordinary leaf-block route calls normal block contents."
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "u-f4008c5f64fc6cb6d4d1",
          "start_line": 4736,
          "end_line": 4743,
          "role": "dependency",
          "dependency_reason": "Normal block contents analyzes and then processes inline marks."
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "u-9854f259ba7c0191d3ec",
          "start_line": 4131,
          "end_line": 4158,
          "role": "dependency",
          "dependency_reason": "Inline analysis collects marks and calls md_analyze_link_contents outside table mode."
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "u-fbbe6bfc649369919054",
          "start_line": 4173,
          "end_line": 4181,
          "role": "dependency",
          "dependency_reason": "Flagged, unresolved two-character pipe marks are sent to md_analyze_pipe."
        }
      ],
      "absence_claim": false,
      "audited_unit_ids": []
    },
    {
      "topic": "consequence",
      "statement": "The after pipe analyzer resolves a paired opener and closer. Inline processing dispatches resolved double-pipe marks as spoiler span callbacks, whose HTML handlers emit opening and closing x-spoiler tags.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "unit_id": "u-aea6042884a3262bb813",
          "start_line": 150,
          "end_line": 154,
          "role": "primary",
          "dependency_reason": ""
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "u-3e73bbc2708be8760b6c",
          "start_line": 3854,
          "end_line": 3869,
          "role": "dependency",
          "dependency_reason": "Pairs and resolves the double-pipe marks."
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "u-2106c93931de3a887955",
          "start_line": 4346,
          "end_line": 4353,
          "role": "dependency",
          "dependency_reason": "Turns the resolved pair into spoiler span callbacks."
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "u-7bb4879720e3cda5d58e",
          "start_line": 467,
          "end_line": 470,
          "role": "dependency",
          "dependency_reason": "The opening callback renders <x-spoiler>."
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "u-078e4f228e76b4cce357",
          "start_line": 1,
          "end_line": 1,
          "role": "dependency",
          "dependency_reason": "The closing callback renders </x-spoiler>."
        }
      ],
      "absence_claim": false,
      "audited_unit_ids": []
    },
    {
      "topic": "counterevidence",
      "statement": "The old entry already supplies the flag and Markdown needed for this spoiler behavior through its md_html call, so its input format does not block the frozen route. Its output callback discards rendered output, and the complete entry contains no assertion about that output.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "unit_id": "u-1056c6fa42072a012709",
          "start_line": 1,
          "end_line": 31,
          "role": "primary",
          "dependency_reason": ""
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "u-48a51db95f89128f1fd3",
          "start_line": 325,
          "end_line": 326,
          "role": "dependency",
          "dependency_reason": "The spoiler flag can be represented by the fuzz-derived parser flag word."
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "u-68abec90fe8e7055cf03",
          "start_line": 541,
          "end_line": 573,
          "role": "dependency",
          "dependency_reason": "md_html forwards those flags and input bytes to the parser."
        }
      ],
      "absence_claim": true,
      "audited_unit_ids": [
        "u-1056c6fa42072a012709"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "missing_information": [],
  "requested_symbols": [],
  "requested_paths": []
}
